nged or new and exit with status 1.\",\"id\":\"new-inputs-not-in-checksum-manifest\",\"location\":\"replication/hash_inputs.py:65-73, replication/input_manifest.md:4-7, replication/README.md:92-95\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"suggested_fix\":\"On Machine A, run python replication/hash_inputs.py to update replication/input_manifest.md with the SHA-256 digests of all 389 inputs, verify the hashes, and commit the updated manifest.\",\"title\":\"The 285 newly added Section 4.3 input files are not recorded in the checksum manifest\",\"what_the_code_does\":\"replication/hash_inputs.py now adds 3 FamilySearch link files and 282 divided-file shards to input_list(), bringing total inputs to 389. However, replication/input_manifest.md still records only 104 files from 2026-11-01. Consequently, python replication/hash_inputs.py --check treats all 285 additions as new or changed and fails.\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Tables 9ΓÇô11 depend on inputs whose cryptographic digests are unrecorded. While README.md describes these files as frozen inputs, neither the authors nor an external replicator can verify the integrity of the files used to produce the Section 4.3 results.\"},{\"confidence\":\"verified\",\"dimension\":\"replication\",\"how_to_check\":\"In python, run: import replication.hash_inputs as h; old=set(h.read_manifest()); cur={h.short(f) for f in h.input_list()}; print(sorted(old-cur)). The current --check loop tests only old.get(short(f)) != digest for f in files, ignoring manifest entries missing from disk. In run_machineA.do:55-61, verify that if a shard is missing, dfiles simply omits it and nmiss remains 0.\",\"id\":\"removed-shards-ignored-by-hash-check\",\"location\":\"replication/hash_inputs.py:68-73, replication/hash_inputs.py:125-133, replication/run_machineA.do:55-61\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"suggested_fix\":\"In hash_inputs.py, verify bidirectional completeness by asserting set(old.keys()) == set(short(f) for f in files) during --check. In run_machineA.do, assert expected shard counts (143 for 1930 and 139 for 1940) rather than dynamically accepting whatever files match norace*.dta.\",\"title\":\"Input preflight and checksum verification fail to detect missing divided-file shards\",\"what_the_code_does\":\"hash_inputs.py discovers divided-file shards using d.glob(\\\"norace*.dta\\\"), and check mode only iterates over existing files. It never checks whether files present in the manifest were removed from disk. Similarly, run_machineA.do gathers shards using dir ... files \\\"norace*.dta\\\"; if a shard is deleted, it is simply omitted from inputs and passes preflight without error.\",\"why_it_matters\":\"If one or more divided-file shards are lost or corrupted, neither the Stata preflight nor hash_inputs.py --check will raise an error. In MATCHING/fs_avg_performance.do and fs_cells.do, missing shards would silently drop records and alter middle-initial validation rates.\"}],\"review_limits\":[\"No paper draft was supplied, so draft text, reported claims, and claims-vs-code language could not be checked.\",\"External census and linkage data files on D:\\\\Dropbox and F:\\\\ were unavailable and the Stata pipeline was not run; data uniqueness, merge results, and runtime numerical values were assessed from source code.\",\"Identification choices (such as evaluating ML models on discordant records or linking via FamilySearch transcriptions) were traced in code, but their treatment and caveats in the paper text could not be evaluated without the draft.\",\"The review was limited to the uncommitted working-tree changes, the newly invoked Section 4.3 scripts (MATCHING/fs_avg_performance.do, MATCHING/fs_cells.do, MATCHING/fs_draft_tables.py), and directly related replication files.\"],\"summary\":\"The Section 4.3 replication pipeline is currently broken because replication/Run-MachineA.ps1 contains an embedded ASCII form-feed byte (0x0C) in the path to MATCHING/fs_draft_tables.py, causing the driver to abort immediately after the len